+ * strings and protocol reply state. Call its reply function at most once, from
+ * the same terminal-owning thread, and then free it. Later VT writes are allowed.
+ * Freeing without replying cancels the request without emitting a response.
+ * Every retained request MUST be freed before terminal reset/destruction.
+ * Failure leaves the original request available for an immediate error reply.
+ * Retaining twice, after replying, or retaining an already retained request is
